# cmd.exe reads a batch file by byte offset and re-seeks after every external
# command it runs. LF-only line endings put those offsets out by one per line,
# and the interpreter ends up resuming in the middle of a later line. Keep the
# wrappers CRLF whatever the checking-out machine is set to.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
